<Layout title="Research" description="Research projects, grants, and infrastructure — radiation belts, ULF waves, GIC forecasting, and space weather ML by Victor A. Pinto Abarzúa.">

<section>
  <h1>Research</h1>
  <p class="lead">
    I lead the <a href="https://heliousach.github.io" target="_blank">HelioFísica and Space Weather Research Group at USACH</a>, focused on Earth's radiation belt dynamics, ULF waves in the solar wind and magnetosphere, and machine learning applications for space weather prediction.
  </p>
</section>

<div class="divider"></div>

<h2>Research Areas</h2>
<div class="section">
  <div class="card">
    <h3>Radiation Belts and Relativistic Electrons</h3>
    <p>Energization and decay of electron radiation belts. Enhancement and dropout events in the outer radiation belt. Formation, evolution, and decay of ultrarelativistic remnant belts. Radial response of relativistic electrons to geomagnetic perturbations.</p>
  </div>
  <div class="card">
    <h3>ULF Waves and Magnetospheric Turbulence</h3>
    <p>Correlation between ULF wave power and changes in relativistic electron fluxes. Propagation of Alfvénic fluctuations from the solar wind to the inner magnetosphere. Turbulence and total pressure balance in the dynamic magnetosphere.</p>
  </div>
  <div class="card">
    <h3>Machine Learning for Space Weather</h3>
    <p>Prediction of ground magnetic field perturbations and geomagnetically induced currents (GIC) using deep neural networks (CNN, RNN, LSTM). Probabilistic forecasting and interpretable models with explainability techniques (Integrated Gradients, Shapley Values).</p>
  </div>
  <div class="card">
    <h3>Solar Wind – Magnetosphere Coupling</h3>
    <p>Solar wind influence on inner magnetospheric dynamics. Geomagnetic storm effects on technology, satellites, and ionospheric disturbances. Particle precipitation into the upper atmosphere.</p>
  </div>
</div>

